# git attributes

# .claude/PROJECT_INDEX.md is generated — `git pushx` regenerates it on every
# feature branch. Two branches touching different source files still produce
# different index content, so a plain 3-way merge reports a CONFLICT on a file
# neither author edited (workspace-1pu). `merge=union` is a BUILT-IN driver, so
# there is no per-clone git config that could be silently absent, and GitHub
# honours it server-side — the PR does not conflict. The index is a line-based
# list, so union keeps shared lines once and both sides' unique entries; the
# next pushx regenerates a clean one. No-op wherever this file does not exist.
.claude/PROJECT_INDEX.md merge=union
